if (getInteractionMode() != ConsoleProcessInfo.INTERACTION_NEVER)
```
Reason:
The fix involves saving the console process before calling `getInteractionMode()`. By ensuring that the console process is set first, the subsequent calls to `getInteractionMode()` will use the correct and initialized console process, thus allowing for accurate computation of the interaction mode.


